================================================================================
Prompt: generate_config.j2
Service Step: GENERATE_CONFIG (AI Creative Generation) / POLISH_CONFIG (AI Targeted Polishing)
Function Summary: Generate a complete creative configuration scheme from user brief descriptions, or perform targeted polishing on existing configurations
Upstream Input:
  - mode: short/long (work mode)
  - mode_label: mode label
  - operation: generate/polish
  - user_hint: user hint
  - current_config_json: current config (polish mode)
  - selected_suggestions/focus_fields: user-selected polishing directions
  - hard_constraints_text: explicit hard parameters specified by user in AI generation popup (genre/tone/length)
  - story_synopsis_impact_text: UI parameter impact on theme/premise implementation requirements
  - output_fields_text: allowed output fields derived by backend from current form template
  - anchor_constraints_text: anti-drift anchor points extracted by backend from current configuration
Downstream Output:
  - JSON: complete creative configuration (theme/premise, genre, characters_hint, etc.)
  - Downstream Consumers:
    * Short Mode: SPEC_ENRICH consumes all fields to generate complete specification, then enters SHORT_BLUEPRINT
    * Long Mode: INIT_STORY_BIBLE consumes premise/world_hint/conflict_hint to generate worldview
                INIT_CHARACTER_BILLBLE consumes premise/characters_hint to generate character profiles
                PLAN_OUTLINE consumes all spec fields to generate narrative blueprint
Consumption Chain Priority:
  P0 = genre/tone enum value correctness / field completeness
  P1 = characters_hint consistency with premise / conflict hierarchy clarity
  P2 = uniqueness / visual imagery / hook density
Brief Example:
  Input: mode="short", theme="memory recycler..."
  Output: {"theme":"...","genre":"scifi","tone":"suspenseful",...}

【Protective Comments - Do Not Delete Following Content】
- The "Creative Quality Requirements" section (uniqueness/visual imagery/conflict hierarchy/character authenticity/hook density) is the core quality standard for creative writing,
  not a field list that repeats the JSON schema. These standards directly affect the quality of the generated configuration scheme; deletion would cause
  output to become "templated," lacking the uniqueness and appeal that creative writing should have.
- In particular, "hook density" (the first sentence of premise/theme must make readers want to continue) and "conflict hierarchy"
  (external suspense drives plot, internal conflict drives character arc) are crucial to story appeal.
- "Genre Awareness" and "Rhythm" requirements for short/long form are also key design intentions, ensuring appropriate structure for different lengths.
- Short form characters_hint must include gender markers (male/female/other); subsequent pronoun consistency checks depend on this information.
- Creative configuration fields must be completely aligned with StorySpec field definitions in core/schemas/spec.py;
  only desktop metadata fields polish_suggestions and creative_note may be additionally output; required fields in schema must not be omitted.
